{# Skills are an ordered list of {label, items} groups, so the categories and
   their order live in the data, not here. Both the headings and the grouping
   change without touching this file.

   One comma-separated paragraph per group, not an \itemize: with the section
   grouped by domain the real CV carries ~65 entries, and one \item per entry
   is ~65 lines -- a full page of single-word bullets that costs a page and
   reads worse than the prose form. \parskip (\cvitemskip) separates the
   groups, matching every other section's rhythm.

   group["items"] is subscripted deliberately: Jinja resolves attributes before
   keys, and on a dict `.items` is the built-in method, so `group.items` would
   silently render a bound method instead of the list. #}
{% for group in skills %}
\textbf{ {{- group.label | latex_escape -}} :} {{ group["items"] | join(', ') | latex_escape }}
{% endfor %}
